      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Qutb-ud-din Aibak was known as 'Lakh Baksh' (Giver of Lakhs) — frequently asked in SSC exams.",
        "Market Control System and price regulation policies were uniquely introduced by Alauddin Khilji.",
        "The token currency experiment and shifting of capital from Delhi to Devagiri (Daulatabad) are key traits of Muhammad bin Tughlaq's reign.",
        "The First Battle of Panipat (1526 CE) between Babur and Ibrahim Lodi marked the transition from the Delhi Sultanate to the Mughal Empire."
